# Code owners: a review from an owning team is required to merge.
# Replace `your-org` with the GitHub organization name.
#
# Order matters: the LAST matching pattern wins, so broad rules come first.
# Team slugs read <section><number>-<domain>, e.g. a3-cat and b3-cat are the
# two teams that share the catalog domain.
#
# Each domain's src/contract.rs is shared by both of its teams. CODEOWNERS
# accepts approval from ANY listed owner, so "both teams approve" for
# contract changes is a review rule (see CONTRIBUTING.md), not enforced here.

# Default: platform teams own everything not claimed below, including the
# workspace manifests, CI, the API server, shared core, the shared API
# client, and the client app shells.
*                                            @your-org/a1-plt @your-org/b1-plt

# identity
/backend/domains/identity/                   @your-org/a2-idn @your-org/b2-idn
/clients/*/src/features/identity/            @your-org/a2-idn @your-org/b2-idn
/clients/mcp/src/tools/identity.ts           @your-org/a2-idn @your-org/b2-idn

